   └─ run it from inside the repo whose file it is

## play.stop · --help
rc=0
usage:
  rhx git.grove.play.stop <grove> --play <name>
  rhx git.grove.play.stop <grove> --play <name> --scratch '.local/state/<prefix>.*'

guarantee:
  - asks over its own ssh, around the pane (as git.grove.play.await does)
  - scoped to the ssh user's own processes; the pattern names the play FILE
  - TERM to the play and each descendant, KILL to any left after 5s
  - --scratch globs are relative to $HOME and must sit under .local/state/
  - reports the processes stopped, the scratch removed, and the disk after
  - a pgrep that cannot answer is no "none ran": it exits 1, as await reads it
  - exit 0 = stopped (or none ran) · 1 = the box or its pgrep did not answer · 2 = bad args

## play.stop · an unknown arg refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: unknown arg '--bogus'
   └─ fix: rhx git.grove.play.stop <grove> --play <name>

## play.stop · two groves refuse
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: two groves named: 'grove-a' and 'grove-b'
   └─ fix: name one: rhx git.grove.play.stop <grove> --play <name>

## reset.probe · --help
rc=0
brains.auth.reset.probe — run the usage-reset reader on one node, and show what jq said

usage:
  rhx brains.auth.reset.probe                      the cli's real-offer shape
  rhx brains.auth.reset.probe --node '<json>' [--kind full|fable]
  rhx brains.auth.reset.probe --from checkout      read this checkout's copy, not ~/

options:
  --node <json>      the usage node to read (default: the real-offer shape)
  --kind full|fable  which reset row to read (default: full)
  --from installed|checkout  whose reader runs (default: installed)

## reset.probe · the default node
rc=0
🔬 brains.auth.reset.probe --kind full --from checkout
   ├─ jq: <jq>
   ├─ reader: 🎁 session reset available now
   └─ jq stderr: (none) ✔

## reset.probe · a node jq cannot parse
rc=0
🔬 brains.auth.reset.probe --kind full --from checkout
   ├─ jq: <jq>
   ├─ reader: ? could not read the reset fields
   └─ jq stderr
      └─ jq: <jq>

## reset.probe · saved grants, the full row
rc=0
🔬 brains.auth.reset.probe --kind full --from checkout
   ├─ jq: <jq>
   ├─ reader: 🎁 3 saved · 2 usable now · first expires dec 01
   └─ jq stderr: (none) ✔

## reset.probe · saved grants, the fable row
rc=0
🔬 brains.auth.reset.probe --kind fable --from checkout
   ├─ jq: <jq>
   ├─ reader: 🎀 1 saved · usable now · expires dec 09
   └─ jq stderr: (none) ✔

## reset.probe · an unknown arg refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: unknown arg: --bogus
   └─ fix: rhx brains.auth.reset.probe --help

## reset.probe · no installed reader refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: no reader at <home>/.bash_aliases.brains.auth.sh

