## reach.set · --help
rc=0
aws.reach.set — give this box one org+env's aws identity, both halves

usage:
  rhx aws.reach.set --org <org> --env <env> [--assume <role>] [--mode apply]

options:
  --org       the org the account belongs to            (required)
  --env       test | prep | prod | camp                 (required)
  --assume    role to assume there                      (required, except --env camp)
              (NOT --role: rhachet injects that into every skill)
  --account   12-digit account id     (read from declapract.use.yml if absent)
  --from      repo path holding declapract.use.yml      (default: cwd)
  --owner     rack owner + profile-name tail            (default: ehmpath)
  --region    aws region                                (default: us-east-1)
  --gitroot   git root for keyrack calls  (default: cwd if a repo, else the rack's)
  --mode      plan (default) or apply

it writes BOTH halves of the pointer:
  1. [profile <org>.<env>.<owner>]  in ~/.aws/config   (the body, per box)
  2. <org>.<env>.AWS_PROFILE        on the rack        (the name, everywhere)

examples:
  rhx aws.reach.set --org ahbode --env test --assume <prep-oidc-role> --mode apply
  rhx aws.reach.set --org ahbode --env camp --mode apply

## reach.del · --help
rc=0
aws.reach.del — take one org+env's reach off this box, both halves

usage:
  rhx aws.reach.del --org <org> --env <env> [--mode apply]

options:
  --org       the org whose reach to remove            (required)
  --env       the env whose reach to remove            (required)
  --owner     rack owner + profile-name tail           (default: ehmpath)
  --gitroot   git root for the keyrack del  (default: cwd if a repo, else the rack's)
  --mode      plan (default) or apply

it removes BOTH halves of the pointer:
  1. [profile <org>.<env>.<owner>]  from ~/.aws/config  (the body)
  2. <org>.<env>.AWS_PROFILE        from the rack       (the name)

🛑 a stale profile is a DECLARATION drift — reap it by the one command:
  rhx grove.provision --what 5.13.reach --mode apply

## reach.set · a --gitroot that is no repo refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: --gitroot '<home>/notrepo' is not a git repo
   fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.12.rack --mode apply   (it owns the rack root)

## reach.del · a --gitroot that is no repo refuses
rc=2
✋ ConstraintError: --gitroot '<home>/notrepo' is not a git repo
   fix: rhx grove.provision --what 5.12.rack --mode apply   (it owns the rack root)

## reach.set · a laptop profile with no sso login refuses
rc=2
🐢 heres the wave...

🔭 aws.reach.set --org ahbode --env test --mode plan
   ├─ profile: ahbode.test.ehmpath
   ├─ box:     laptop (local@unix — no platform identity)
   └─ ✋ ConstraintError: a laptop, and 'ahbode.test.ehmpath' is NOT declared
      ├─ why: on a laptop this profile is an sso login, whose sso_start_url this skill has no truthful source for
      └─ fix: declare it with aws's own tool, then rerun this to set the rack half: aws configure sso --profile ahbode.test.ehmpath

## reach.set · a laptop profile already declared needs no work
rc=0
🐢 heres the wave...

🔭 aws.reach.set --org ahbode --env test --mode plan
   ├─ profile: ahbode.test.ehmpath
   ├─ box:     laptop (local@unix — no platform identity)
   └─ ✔ a laptop, and 'ahbode.test.ehmpath' is already declared — no work
      ├─ a laptop's body is an sso login, owned by 'aws configure sso'; this skill authors grove bodies
      └─ prove it: aws sts get-caller-identity --profile ahbode.test.ehmpath

